<!--
  Ship UI landing — the umbrella front door. Generic across the four products
  (SUI · Deck · Components · AI), not a SUI-only pitch. Renders full-width (no
  sidebar) like the SolidJS/Svelte landings; the docs sections carry the sidebar.
-->
<div class="landing-wrap">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">SHIP UI · 0.2.0</p>
    <h1>The UI stack for <span class="grad">agent-built apps</span>.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A compiler-first component framework, an app framework, a batteries-included
      component library, and agent tooling — built to produce correct, on-brand
      custom UI fast. Author close to HTML, TS, and CSS; the compiler enforces the
      design system and emits standard web components.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/getting-started">Get started</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/tutorial">Try the tutorial</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="products">
    <a class="product-card" href="/getting-started">
      <h3>SUI <span class="tag">framework</span></h3>
      <p>The reactive component framework. Signals and a strict lint, compiled ahead-of-time to standard web components.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="product-card" href="/deck">
      <h3>Deck <span class="tag">app framework</span></h3>
      <p>Routing, server rendering with hydration, bundling, live data, and a hot-reloading dev loop — driving the compiler for you.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="product-card" href="/components">
      <h3>Components <span class="tag">library</span></h3>
      <p>Around 74 accessible, on-brand primitives — the batteries the framework composes from.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="product-card" href="/ai">
      <h3>AI <span class="tag">agent-first</span></h3>
      <p>Built to be authored by agents: strict compile-time guardrails, MCP tooling, and a scored authoring eval.</p>
    </a>
  </section>
</div>
